  "notes": {
    "switchingFrequency": "Programmable with an RON resistor. The Recommended Operating Conditions give a maximum of 1000 kHz and no minimum, which is what \"Adjustable switching frequency up to 1MHz\" on page 1 says too.",
    "voutMax": "Not stated. The output is set by an external divider from the 1.2 V reference, and no table gives an upper end.",
    "ioutMax": "The 1 A in the title. The Recommended Operating Conditions table shows a load current maximum of 1.25 A.",
    "lightLoadMode": "Diode emulation: the low-side FET is turned off when the inductor current reaches zero, so the part skips cycles at light load. Recorded as pfm rather than psm because the datasheet names the mechanism, not a pulse-skipping mode.",
    "maxDutyCycle": "Not stated as a percentage. The constraint is expressed as a minimum off-time of 50 ns (page 13) and a programmable on-time range.",
    "efficiencyPeak": "Given only as curves in the Typical Characteristics, with no peak stated in text.",
    "feedbackAccuracy": "Arithmetic on the stated limits: 1.218 V and 1.181 V about 1.2 V is about +/-1.5%. The datasheet states the limits, not the percentage."
  },
